  "limitations": [
    "Help receipt (HAALSI) and help need/inability (CLHLS) differ.",
    "No-help requires all included activities negative; any positive suffices despite another item missing. Otherwise unknown.",
    "Eating screen-negative (PF013=2) with missing PF014 is coded negative using skip logic. Other missing help stays unknown. W4 questionnaire documents the skip; W2 raw patterns are consistent with that routing. Broad sensitivity includes cannot-do responses.",
    "Baseline-reference standardization recalculated using five-item baseline-negative score-complete pool; fixed original SD comparison also reported.",
    "Death, missing outcome and missing marker scores never imputed.",
    "Unweighted conditional association among observed participants, not causal effects or population incidence.",
    "Original historical screening q values cannot be carried over to the new five-item analysis. New p values are nominal and exploratory."
